  {
   "id": "intro",
   "type": "intro",
   "heading": {
    "en": "When there is nothing left to say"
   },
   "hook": {
    "en": "The mother once laughed at this photograph. Now her child holds it, and cannot laugh at all."
   },
   "objectives": [
    {
     "en": "Explain the situation in the final stanza"
    },
    {
     "en": "Compare the mother's loss with the speaker's loss"
    },
    {
     "en": "Interpret the idea of silence in the poem"
    }
   ],
   "narration": {
    "en": "The mother once laughed at this photograph. Now her child holds it, and cannot laugh at all."
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "concept1",
   "type": "concept",
   "title": {
    "en": "The final stanza"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "The final stanza returns to the present. The mother has now been dead for nearly as many years as the girl in the photograph had lived, that is, about twelve years. The mother could laugh at her lost childhood, but the speaker cannot laugh at this loss. The speaker has nothing to say about the situation: the mother's death has left a silence so heavy that it silences the speaker too."
   },
   "points": [
    {
     "en": "The mother has been dead about twelve years"
    },
    {
     "en": "The mother's loss: her childhood"
    },
    {
     "en": "The speaker's loss: the mother herself"
    },
    {
     "en": "\"Its silence silences\": grief beyond words"
    }
   ],
   "narration": {
    "en": "The final stanza returns to the present. The mother has now been dead for nearly as many years as the girl in the photograph had lived, that is, about twelve years. The mother could laugh at her lost childhood, but the speaker cannot laugh at this loss. The speaker has nothing to say about the situation: the mother's death has left a silence so heavy that it silences the speaker too."
   }
